form=\"translate(2683.4,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-29\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(422,363) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"2F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(4216.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"3B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3B\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mtd\" transform=\"translate(5494.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D465\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D465\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(849.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"2265\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2265\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1905.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2405.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"2E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2E\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(8927.7,0) translate(0 250)\"></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>Then the number of points, where the function <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.464ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.467ex\" height=\"2.059ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1974.4 910\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D454\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D454\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(702.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2218\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2218\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1424.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D453\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D453\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> is discontinuous, is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.14ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.525ex\" height=\"0.084ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 25 2000 37\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"5F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-5F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"5F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-5F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"><use data-c=\"5F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-5F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1500,0)\"><use data-c=\"5F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-5F\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> .</p>","options":[],"correct_options":[],"answer":"3","explanation":"<p>We need to find the points where the composite function $g \\circ f$ is discontinuous.</p>\n<p>That means we first find</p>\n<p>$$ (g \\circ f)(x)=g(f(x)). $$</p>\n<p>So we must see, for each value of $x$, which branch of $g$ will be used.</p>\n\n<h2>1. Given functions</h2>\n<p>$$ f(x)= \\begin{cases} x^3+8, & x<0,\\\\ x^2-4, & x\\ge 0 \\end{cases} $$</p>\n<p>and</p>\n<p>$$ g(x)= \\begin{cases} (x-8)^{1/3}, & x<0,\\\\ (x+4)^{1/2}, & x\\ge 0. \\end{cases} $$</p>\n<p>Now,</p>\n<p>$$ (g\\circ f)(x)=g(f(x)). $$</p>\n<p>The definition of $g$ depends on whether its input is negative or non-negative. So we must check the sign of $f(x)$.</p>\n\n<h2>2. Find where $f(x)<0$ and where $f(x)\\ge 0$</h2>\n<h3>Case 1: $x<0$</h3>\n<p>Then</p>\n<p>$$ f(x)=x^3+8. $$</p>\n<p>We check when this is negative:</p>\n<p>$$ x^3+8<0 \\implies x^3<-8 \\implies x<-2. $$</p>\n<p>So for $x<0$:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>if $x<-2$, then $f(x)<0$,</p></li>\n<li><p>if $-2\\le x<0$, then $f(x)\\ge 0$.</p></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Case 2: $x\\ge 0$</h3>\n<p>Then</p>\n<p>$$ f(x)=x^2-4. $$</p>\n<p>We check when this is negative:</p>\n<p>$$ x^2-4<0 \\implies x^2<4 \\implies -2<x<2. $$</p>\n<p>But here $x\\ge 0$, so this becomes</p>\n<p>$$ 0\\le x<2. $$</p>\n<p>Thus for $x\\ge 0$:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>if $0\\le x<2$, then $f(x)<0$,</p></li>\n<li><p>if $x\\ge 2$, then $f(x)\\ge 0$.</p></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>3. Write $(g\\circ f)(x)$ piecewise</h2>\n<p>Now use the correct branch of $g$.</p>\n<h3>(i) When $x<-2$</h3>\n<p>Here $f(x)<0$, so use</p>\n<p>$$ g(y)=(y-8)^{1/3}. $$</p>\n<p>Thus</p>\n<p>$$ (g\\circ f)(x)=\\big((x^3+8)-8\\big)^{1/3}=(x^3)^{1/3}=x. $$</p>\n<p>So for $x<-2$,</p>\n<p>$$ (g\\circ f)(x)=x. $$</p>\n\n<h3>(ii) When $-2\\le x<0$</h3>\n<p>Here $f(x)\\ge 0$, so use</p>\n<p>$$ g(y)=\\sqrt{y+4}. $$</p>\n<p>Thus</p>\n<p>$$ (g\\circ f)(x)=\\sqrt{(x^3+8)+4}=\\sqrt{x^3+12}. $$</p>\n<p>So for $-2\\le x<0$,</p>\n<p>$$ (g\\circ f)(x)=\\sqrt{x^3+12}. $$</p>\n\n<h3>(iii) When $0\\le x<2$</h3>\n<p>Here $f(x)<0$, so use</p>\n<p>$$ g(y)=(y-8)^{1/3}. $$</p>\n<p>Thus</p>\n<p>$$ (g\\circ f)(x)=\\big((x^2-4)-8\\big)^{1/3}=(x^2-12)^{1/3}. $$</p>\n<p>So for $0\\le x<2$,</p>\n<p>$$ (g\\circ f)(x)=(x^2-12)^{1/3}. $$</p>\n\n<h3>(iv) When $x\\ge 2$</h3>\n<p>Here $f(x)\\ge 0$, so use</p>\n<p>$$ g(y)=\\sqrt{y+4}. $$</p>\n<p>Thus</p>\n<p>$$ (g\\circ f)(x)=\\sqrt{(x^2-4)+4}=\\sqrt{x^2}=x $$</p>\n<p>since $x\\ge 2$.</p>\n<p>So for $x\\ge 2$,</p>\n<p>$$ (g\\circ f)(x)=x. $$</p>\n\n<h2>4. Check continuity at possible boundary points</h2>\n<p>Each expression is continuous in its own interval. So we only check the joining points:</p>\n<p>$$ x=-2,\\quad x=0,\\quad x=2. $$</p>\n\n<h3>At $x=-2$</h3>\n<p>Left-hand limit:</p>\n<p>for $x<-2$, $(g\\circ f)(x)=x$, so</p>\n<p>$$ \\lim_{x\\to -2^-}(g\\circ f)(x)=-2. $$</p>\n<p>Right-hand limit:</p>\n<p>for $-2\\le x<0$, $(g\\circ f)(x)=\\sqrt{x^3+12}$, so</p>\n<p>$$ \\lim_{x\\to -2^+}(g\\circ f)(x)=\\sqrt{(-2)^3+12}=\\sqrt{4}=2. $$</p>\n<p>Since</p>\n<p>$$ -2\\ne 2, $$</p>\n<p>the function is discontinuous at $x=-2$.</p>\n\n<h3>At $x=0$</h3>\n<p>Left-hand limit:</p>\n<p>$$ \\lim_{x\\to 0^-}(g\\circ f)(x)=\\sqrt{0^3+12}=\\sqrt{12}. $$</p>\n<p>Right-hand limit:</p>\n<p>$$ \\lim_{x\\to 0^+}(g\\circ f)(x)=(0^2-12)^{1/3}=(-12)^{1/3}. $$</p>\n<p>These are not equal, so discontinuous at $x=0$.</p>\n\n<h3>At $x=2$</h3>\n<p>Left-hand limit:</p>\n<p>$$ \\lim_{x\\to 2^-}(g\\circ f)(x)=(2^2-12)^{1/3}=(-8)^{1/3}=-2. $$</p>\n<p>Right-hand limit:</p>\n<p>$$ \\lim_{x\\to 2^+}(g\\circ f)(x)=2. $$</p>\n<p>These are not equal, so discontinuous at $x=2$.</p>\n\n<h2>5. Conclusion</h2>\n<p>The function $g\\circ f$ is discontinuous at</p>\n<p>$$ x=-2,\\quad x=0,\\quad x=2. $$</p>\n<p>Hence, the number of points of discontinuity is</p>\n<p>$$ \\boxed{3}. $$</p></x></p>"},"hi":{"direction":null,"comprehension":null,"content":"<p>माना <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -2.827ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"26.815ex\" height=\"6.785ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1749.5 11852.1 2999\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D453\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D453\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(550,0)\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(939,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D465\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D465\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1511,0)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-29\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2177.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(3233.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0 -0.5)\"><use data-c=\"7B\" xlink:href=\